comments.body:
@subhash-halder This leads again to the topic discussed above: The axis crossing should be the start of the range - Zero in most cases or 20 in the diagram above. Can you state any reason why it is currently designed like this?

- *developer perspective*: it makes the code a lot more complicated
- *user perspective*: How this gap between the axis crossing and the range start (20 in the diagram above) has to be interpreted? If a categry has a value of 20 than the range should start at 15 or 18. It is not the task of an axis to make sure that minimum value can be displayed.
